From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Builder <builder@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/meson: resync HDMITX after hotplug

The HDMITX hotplug worker disables the output before notifying DRM when HPD
goes low. On systems using the no-HDCP compatibility path, however, the DRM
HPD callback leaves hdmitx_on set and atomic check refuses to force a modeset.
A same-mode reconnect can therefore leave DRM reporting an active connector
while the HDMITX hardware remains disabled.

Always invalidate hdmitx_on after disconnect, independently of the HDCP path,
and force the next modeset-capable commit to re-enable the encoder. Keep HDCP
teardown conditional on the non-Android path as before.
---
--- a/common_drivers/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c
+++ b/common_drivers/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c
@@ -1309,7 +1309,7 @@ int meson_hdmitx_atomic_check(struct drm_connector *connector,
 #endif
 
 	if (state->allow_modeset && new_crtc_state) {
-		if (!am_hdmi->hdmitx_on && !am_hdmi->android_path) {
+		if (!am_hdmi->hdmitx_on) {
 			new_crtc_state->connectors_changed = true;
 			DRM_ERROR("hdmitx_on changed, force modeset.\n");
 		}
@@ -2723,9 +2723,10 @@ static void meson_hdmitx_hpd_cb(void *data)
 	if (hdmitx_get_hpd_state(tx_comm))
 		am_hdmi->odroid_hpd_seen = true;
 #endif
-	if (!hdmitx_get_hpd_state(tx_comm) && !am_hdmi->android_path) {
+	if (!hdmitx_get_hpd_state(tx_comm)) {
 		drm_modeset_lock(mode_lock, NULL);
-		meson_hdmitx_disconnect_hdcp(am_hdmi);
+		if (!am_hdmi->android_path)
+			meson_hdmitx_disconnect_hdcp(am_hdmi);
 		am_hdmi->hdmitx_on = 0;
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_MESON_ODROID_COMMON
 		am_hdmi->uboot_reuse_consumed = true;
